.TH "WEBGL_LOSE_CONTEXT.LOSECONTEXT" "3JS" "April 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WEBGL_lose_context.loseContext \- WEBGL_lose_context: loseContext()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]loseContext()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]WEBGL_lose_context\f[R] extension is part of the WebGL API and
allows you to simulate losing the context of a
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext\f[R].
.PP
It triggers the \c
.UR https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/specs/latest/1.0/#5.15.2
steps described in the WebGL specification
.UE \c
\ for handling context lost.
The context will remain lost until
\f[CR]WEBGL_lose_context.restoreContext()\f[R] is called.
It also destroys the underlying graphics context and all graphics
resources.
This is the recommended mechanism for applications to programmatically
halt their use of the WebGL API.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
loseContext()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
With this method, you can simulate the \f[CR]webglcontextlost\f[R]
event:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] canvas = document.getElementById(\(dqcanvas\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] gl = canvas.getContext(\(dqwebgl\(dq);

canvas.addEventListener(\(dqwebglcontextlost\(dq, (e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(e);
});

gl.getExtension(\(dqWEBGL_lose_context\(dq).loseContext();

\f[I]// WebGLContextEvent event with type \(dqwebglcontextlost\(dq is logged.\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.isContextLost()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Events: \f[CR]webglcontextlost\f[R], \f[CR]webglcontextrestored\f[R],
\f[CR]webglcontextcreationerror\f[R]
